    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Losartan is an angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) used to treat high blood pressure, protect the kidneys, and lower the risk of stroke. While many people tolerate it well, it can cause several common and serious side effects.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most mild side effects happen during the first 1 to 2 weeks and often improve as your body adjusts:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Dizziness or lightheadedness (especially when standing up quickly due to lowered blood pressure)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fatigue or unusual tiredness"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mild headache"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Nausea or mild stomach upset / abdominal pain"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Nasal congestion or upper respiratory symptoms"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Back or joint pain"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Contact a doctor or seek immediate medical care if you experience any of these severe reactions:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "High blood potassium (Hyperkalemia): Signs include muscle weakness, confusion, slow or irregular heartbeat, or numbness and tingling.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Severe low blood pressure (Hypotension): Fainting, severe dizziness, or extreme lightheadedness.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Kidney problems: Sudden unexplained weight gain, swelling in your hands, ankles, or feet, or changes in how much or how often you urinate.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              6,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Severe allergic reaction (Anaphylaxis): Hives, rash, peeling skin, or swelling of the face, lips, tongue, or throat, alongside trouble breathing or swallowing.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Boxed Warning / Pregnancy Risk: Losartan can cause serious harm or death to an unborn baby. It must not be taken during pregnancy."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6,
          10,
          11
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you or someone you know is taking losartan, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Which side effects you are experiencing"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How long you have been taking the medication"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help provide more specific context or direct you on when to call your healthcare provider."
      }
    ],
